# PitWall — AI Agent Rules

## Context
Full project plan lives at docs/pitwall-plan.md — read it before generating 
any code. This is a hackathon MVP with a LOCKED scope. Do not deviate.

## Hard Rules
- Never add features from the "Do not build first" list in the plan 
  (haptics, OLED, LLM coaching, multiple tracks, AI ghosts) without explicit approval.
- Follow the folder structure in section 18 of the plan exactly.
- Use the data model in section 19 exactly (field names, types) unless I approve a change.
- Config values (thresholds, corner definitions) go in config/*.yaml, never hardcoded.
- Coaching output uses only the fixed templates in section 12. No free-form LLM text.
- Rule-based metrics engine must work independently of Edge Impulse at all times.
- Follow current F1 25 UDP telemetry spec (v3 PDF from EA forums) — do not assume 
  field layout from older F1 game years.
- Follow current Arduino UNO Q Bridge API (arduino.app_utils, Bridge.call/provide) — 
  do not use deprecated Bridge Tool syntax from older Arduino boards.

## Workflow
- Small, testable commits. One exit criterion per commit where possible.
- Ask me before introducing a new external Python package.
- If something in docs/pitwall-plan.md conflicts with current official docs 
  (Arduino, Edge Impulse, EA), flag it — don't silently pick one.